cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rootstock Core in research or practice, please cite this software."
title: "Rootstock Core: macOS Security Boundary Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Spicker
    given-names: Sebastian J.
version: 0.1.0-alpha.1
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastianspicker/rootstock"
url: "https://github.com/sebastianspicker/rootstock"
abstract: >-
  This citation record covers the Rootstock Core alpha candidate: a passive,
  local-first workflow that maps macOS security boundaries into an inspectable
  graph. Rootstock Red, Rootstock Blue, and RootstockMacFacts are separate
  components in the same repository and are not covered by this record.
keywords:
  - macOS
  - security
  - attack paths
  - TCC
  - Neo4j
